// BT-3550: Fixture for `Behaviour>>fieldKinds` / `allFieldKinds` BUnit
// coverage (ADR 0124 §9/B5b). One `late` instance slot and one ordinary
// (eager) one, on a plain `Actor subclass:` — mirrors the `CodexClient`
// shape from docs/beamtalk-language-features.md's `late` Slots section,
// without that example's `typed`/`Subprocess` dependencies. No instance of
// this class is ever spawned; field_kinds_test.bt only exercises
// class-level reflection (`fieldKinds`/`allFieldKinds`), which never reads
// `proc`'s (unassigned) value.
//
// See fixtures/late_field_kinds_sub.bt for the subclass fixture used to
// test that an inherited `late` slot appears in `allFieldKinds` but not in
// the subclass's own (local-only) `fieldKinds`.

Actor subclass: LateFieldKindsBase
  late state: proc :: Integer
  state: nextId :: Integer = 0
